stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB

    state "installed" as Installed
    state "checking releases/latest" as Checking
    state "up to date" as Current
    state "system owned path" as Refused
    state "cargo install (compiles)" as CargoInstall
    state "report only, --check" as Reporting
    state "downloading both assets" as Downloading
    state "aborted, nothing replaced" as Aborted
    state "staged and verified" as Staged
    state "hyprlayd quit" as DaemonQuit
    state "hyprlayd.exe replaced" as DaemonReplaced
    state "hyprlay.exe replaced by self-replace" as CliReplaced
    state "Startup entry refreshed" as Refreshing
    state "updated, no Startup entry" as NoService
    state "updated" as Updated
    state "swap failed" as SwapFailed

    [*] --> Installed
    Installed --> Checking : hyprlay update
    Checking --> CargoInstall : path owned by cargo
    Checking --> Refused : path owned by the package manager
    Checking --> Reporting : --check
    Checking --> Current : tag is not newer
    Checking --> Downloading : newer tag
    Downloading --> Aborted : network or digest failure
    Downloading --> Staged : both digests match

    Staged --> DaemonQuit : socket quit, best effort
    DaemonQuit --> DaemonReplaced : rename hyprlayd.exe
    DaemonReplaced --> SwapFailed : image still locked
    DaemonReplaced --> CliReplaced : self-replace hyprlay.exe
    CliReplaced --> SwapFailed : tray holds hyprlay.exe
    CliReplaced --> Refreshing : Startup entry present
    CliReplaced --> NoService : no Startup entry
    Refreshing --> Updated : rewrite script + spawn hyprlayd
    NoService --> Updated : prints run hyprlay install
    CargoInstall --> Updated : cargo rebuilds both, Startup entry refreshed
    Updated --> [*]

    note right of DaemonReplaced
        Windows locks a running image, so the daemon is quit first
        and the rename retries 20 times at 100 ms.
    end note
